 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system as the \"North Dansville Veterans Memorial Highway\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S7281",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7281-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-l, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7281\n\nSPONSOR: BORRELLO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"North Dansville Veterans Memorial High-\nway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nDesignates State Route 63 in the Town of North Dansville, County Living-\nston, as the \"North Dansville Veterans Memorial Highway\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Outlines the new section 344-1 of the highway law to read as\nfollows:  344-1. Portion of the state highway system to be designated as\nthe \"North Dansville Veterans Memorial Highway\". All that portion of the\nstate highway system constituting state route sixty-three in the town of\nNorth Dansville, county of Livingston, shall be designated and known as\nthe \"North Dansville Veterans Memorial Highway\".\n\nSection 2. Indicates that the commissioner of transportation shall\nprovide for the installation and maintenance of adequate signing of the\nstate highway system. Also notes the naming of the route is ceremonial\nin nature.\n\nSection 3. Provides the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town of North Dansville has expressed its desire to honor all those\nwho served in our Armed Forces from the Town of North Dansville. The\nTown Board, by unanimous vote, adopted a formal resolution in 2018\nrequesting legislation to designate New York State Route 63 in the Town\nof North Dansville, Livingston County, as the \"North Dansville Veterans\nMemorial Highway.\" New York State has a long history of recognizing the\nvaliant actions of its veterans, as well as their brave and honorable\nservice and sacrifice. This legislation will rightfully honor veterans\nboth living and deceased in the Town of North Dansville.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: S.6392/A.8156 Referred to Rules/Passed Assembly\n\n2018: S.9151/A.11333 Referred to Rules\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
